        "payload": "tree a0f1c1dd2906c9cdbb1c224dcab05580729f3cd4\nparent a773e1e33b349dc819b5a0edc1c7a4839dc73b48\nauthor Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1791459534 +0200\ncommitter Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1792840273 +0200\n\ndescriptor, rpc, wallet: do not echo key material in error messages\n\nSeveral error messages quote text from the descriptor the caller sent,\nand that text can be a private key. Error text is often logged or\nshared where the request is not. Even the first characters of a key\ngive away part of it.\n\nParsing (src/script/descriptor.cpp, src/util/bip32.cpp):\n- \"Key '%s' is invalid due to whitespace\", \"key '%s' is not valid\" and\n  \"Pubkey '%s' is invalid\" quoted the key. They quote nothing now.\n- \"Multi threshold '%s' is not valid\" and the multipath message \"Key\n  path value '%s' specifies multipath ...\" quote their text only if it\n  is no longer than 11 characters, the length of \"4294967295h\". No key\n  is that short. Longer text is left out.\n- \"Key path value '%s' is not a valid uint32\" follows the same rule.\n- \"'%s' is not a valid descriptor function\" quotes the function name, the\n  text up to '(', followed by \"(...\", as in \"'pk(...' is not a valid\n  descriptor function\". It does so only if the name is 16 characters or\n  fewer. Otherwise, and for a bare key with no '(', nothing is quoted,\n  and the message reads \"Not a valid descriptor function\".\n\nCallers (src/rpc/util.cpp, src/wallet/imports.cpp,\nsrc/wallet/rpc/spend.cpp):\n- \"Cannot derive script without private keys\" and \"Could not add\n  descriptor\" quote desc->ToString(), the public form, instead of the\n  string sent.\n- \"Unable to parse descriptor\" no longer quotes the string. No parsed\n  descriptor exists there, and the parse error says what is wrong.\n\nTests are updated for the new messages. New tests check that no part of\na key is in the parse errors and the caller errors, including a key with\na typo in its last character. They also check the exact text of the\ncaller errors.\n",
